+// [Android AAA perf] CPU topology-aware thread placement for big.LITTLE SoCs.
+// On modest devices (e.g. Snapdragon 695: 2x Cortex-A78 + 6x Cortex-A55) the
+// OS scheduler may place latency-critical emulation threads on the
+// efficiency cores, where single-thread performance is 3-4x lower -
+// catastrophic for the guest main thread and the GPU command processor
+// worker. These helpers classify cores by their
+// /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq/cpuinfo_max_freq (a cluster split
+// around the frequency median; homogeneous systems get no pinning at all)
+// and pin the CALLING thread to the appropriate cluster. Returns true if
+// the affinity was applied; a no-op (false) on failure, on homogeneous
+// parts, and on platforms without sched_setaffinity.
+bool PinCurrentThreadToPerformanceCores();
+bool PinCurrentThreadToEfficiencyCores();
+
+// [Android AAA perf] Lowers the calling thread's OS scheduling priority
+// (setpriority +10) so background threads (async pipeline compilation,
+// audio, vblank) do not compete with the game's threads for big cores.
+// Unprivileged processes may only lower priority, so this can never fail
+// in a harmful direction; returns true if applied.
+bool DemoteCurrentThreadPriority();
+
 // Enables the current process to set thread affinity.
 // Must be called at startup before attempting to set thread affinity.
 void EnableAffinityConfiguration();
